[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Queen's Gambit Declined"]
[Variation "Bf4 Variation"]
[ECO "D37"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "early-c5,symmetrical-centre"]
[Kind "sideline"]

1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. Bf4 { Develops the bishop outside the pawn chain, so no pin on f6 to worry about. }
4... Be7 5. e3 O-O 6. Nf3 c5 { With the bishop on f4 and no pin, Black can hit the centre at once. Opening the position
helps the side with the more compact pawns. } 7. dxc5 ( 7. cxd5 exd5 8. dxc5 Bxc5 ) ( 7. Be2 cxd4 8. exd4 Nc6 ) 7... Bxc5
{ Takes the pawn back with a developing move. } 8. Qc2 Nc6 9. a3 Bd6 { Offers to swap off White's active bishop. } 10.
Bxd6 Qxd6 { Black has equal chances; the pawns on d5 and e6 are healthy and all the pieces are active. } *
